eviewDetail.tsx to use apiClient\n   596→  - id: tests-agent\n   597→    scope: pytest and vitest test suites for all iter-4 biomes\n   598→    branch: feat/tests-agent\n   599→    blocked_by:\n   600→      - discover-agent\n   601→      - scheduler-agent\n   602→      - api-streaming-agent\n   603→      - api-client-agent\n   604→    blocks: []\n   605→    capabilities:\n   606→      - pytest\n   607→      - vitest\n   608→      - fakeredis\n   609→    sub_agents:\n   610→      - id: tests-agent.discovery.pubsub\n   611→        scope: tests/discovery/test_orchestrator_pubsub.py — fake Redis, verify 8+ event\n   612→          sequence\n   613→      - id: tests-agent.scheduler.daily\n   614→        scope: tests/scheduler/test_daily_task.py — mock orchestrator, verify crawl_runs\n   615→          creation\n   616→      - id: tests-agent.api.events\n   617→        scope: tests/api/test_events_stream.py — TestClient streaming, verify SSE frames\n   618→          + heartbeat\n   619→      - id: tests-agent.api.review\n   620→        scope: tests/api/test_review_approve.py — full integration approve flow\n   621→      - id: tests-agent.frontend.client\n   622→        scope: frontend/src/api/__tests__/client.test.ts — vitest, mock fetch, 401\n   623→          handling\n   624→merge_order:\n   625→  - data-agent\n   626→  - design-agent\n   627→  - auth-agent\n   628→  - obs-agent\n   629→  - discover-agent\n   630→  - apply-agent\n   631→  - agents-agent\n   632→  - api-agent\n   633→  - scheduler-agent\n   634→  - api-streaming-agent\n   635→  - frontend-agent\n   636→  - api-client-agent\n   637→  - infra-agent\n   638→  - tests-agent\n   639→timeline:\n   640→  parallel_phases:\n   641→    - hours: 0-1\n   642→      active:\n   643→        - data-agent\n   644→        - design-agent\n   645→      description: Wave 1 — foundations with zero cross-biome deps. Schemas + models +\n   646→        design tokens land first so every downstream biome consumes frozen\n   647→        contracts.\n   648→    - hours: 1-3\n   649→      active:\n   650→        - auth-agent\n   651→        - obs-agent\n   652→      description: Wave 2 — core services depending only on data. Auth + observability\n   653→        wire on top of the schema, both consumed by every engine below.\n   654→    - hours: 3-5\n   655→      active:\n   656→        - discover-agent\n   657→      description: Wave 3a — Discovery engine with pub/sub gap closure. Must publish\n   658→        events on agent.status.discovery channel.\n   659→    - hours: 5-7\n   660→      active:\n   661→        - scheduler-agent\n   662→        - api-streaming-agent\n   663→      description: Wave 3b — Scheduler and streaming in parallel. Scheduler consumes\n   664→        discover-agent, streaming consumes obs-agent.\n   665→    - hours: 7-8\n   666→      active:\n   667→        - apply-agent\n   668→      description: Wave 4 — Application engine, blocked by discover-agent.\n   669→    - hours: 8-9\n   670→      active:\n   671→        - agents-agent\n   672→      description: Wave 5 — AgentManager wrapper over the engines.\n   673→    - hours: 9-11\n   674→      active:\n   675→        - api-agent\n   676→        - frontend-agent\n   677→      description: Wave 6 — Surfaces. API + frontend land in parallel.\n   678→    - hours: 11-12\n   679→      active:\n   680→        - api-client-agent\n   681→      description: Wave 7 — Frontend API wiring, blocked by api-agent + api-streaming-agent.\n   682→    - hours: 12-13\n   683→      active:\n   684→        - infra-agent\n   685→      description: Wave 8 — Deploy. Docker + ECS + Digital Dash pipeline with Celery\n   686→        containers.\n   687→    - hours: 13-14\n   688→      active:\n   689→        - tests-agent\n   690→      description: Wave 9 — Test sweep across all iter-4 biomes.\n   691→budget:\n   692→  maxUsd: 100\n   693→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN 